# Checked-in DERIVED artifacts — regenerated from source, never hand-edited.
#
#   processos/assets/ir.gbnf  emitted by `cd processos && cargo run -- emit-gbnf`.
#
# (engine-wasm/pkg used to be listed here; it is no longer committed — it is a
# gitignored build output built by `make console-wasm` and by CI, #668.)
#
# Two consequences:
#
#  1. linguist-generated — collapse it in GitHub PR diffs, so a review sees the
#     source change, not the regenerated grammar.
#
#  2. merge=keep-ours — never attempt a three-way merge of the artifact. The
#     authoritative bytes are not merged — they are REGENERATED against the
#     merged source, and the processos test suite regenerates the grammar in
#     memory and asserts it equals the checked-in file (the
#     `checked_in_grammar_matches_emitter` parity test), so a stale commit fails
#     the build.
#
# The `keep-ours` driver is registered by `make setup` (`git config
# merge.keep-ours.driver true`). Git silently ignores an unregistered driver and
# falls back to a manual conflict resolve, so this degrades gracefully in a
# clone that has not run setup.
processos/assets/ir.gbnf      linguist-generated=true merge=keep-ours
